  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/">Remark <span data-tag="">6.5.0.1</span>.</a>The Brown-Joyal-Jardine theory of simplicial (pre)sheaves on a topological space $X$ is a model for the hypercomplete $\infty $-topos $\Shv (X)^{\wedge }$. In many respects, the $\infty $-topos $\Shv (X)$ of sheaves of spaces on $X$ is better behaved <em>before</em> hypercompletion. We will outline some of the advantages of $\Shv (X)$ in §<a href="/tag/77791A" data-tag="77791A">6.5.4</a> and in §<a href="/tag/5BFAA3" data-tag="5BFAA3">7</a>. </p>
